<title>USA: US Navy prepares to split contracts on destroyers.</title>
<headline>US Navy prepares to split contracts on destroyers.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Navy announced early letter contract awards of up to $164.7 million each to the Bath Iron Works unit of General Dynamics Corp and Ingalls Shipbuilding unit of Litton Industries for construction of a total of 12 Arleigh Burke class destroyers.</p>
<p>The money would be for early advanced procurement work on the 12 Aegis destroyers to be built over the coming decade.</p>
<p>Plans are for the Bath shipyard in Maine and Ingalls in Louisana to divide work on the 12 ships.</p>
</text>
